  "body": "## What happens\n\nThe Mazak post never writes `G94`. Each F word is a feed per minute (mm/min or in/min). A control setting selects `G94` or `G95` at power-on and at reset, and an earlier program or MDI can leave `G95` active. In `G95`, the control reads `F1200` as 1200 mm per revolution.\n\n## Expected\n\nThe post writes `G94` before the first F word: with the modal words of the section preamble, or once at program start.\n\n## Evidence (upstream main `eafe6aec6`)\n\n- `assets/posts/mazak.cps:460-470`: `onOpen` and `unitBlock` write no `G94`.\n- `assets/posts/mazak.cps:591`: the preamble `G17 G90 G54 G40 G49 G80` has no `G94`.\n- No line of `mazak.cps` writes `G94` or `G95`.\n- Related: #4150 (the same gap in the Sinumerik 840D preamble).\n\nWorkaround: the operator makes sure that the control is in `G94` before cycle start.\n\nFound by the post audit against the Mazak manuals (#4130).\n\n## Done means\n\nThe Mazak goldens show `G94` before the first F word. A test pins it.\n",
